# PLAN.md — FormCoach

---

## Definition of Done (every slice must pass all of these before moving on)

1. **No console errors** — no red-text errors or unhandled promise rejections in the Metro terminal or device logs.
2. **Smallest supported screen** — tested on an **iPhone SE (2nd gen) simulator** (375 pt wide × 667 pt tall) or a real iPhone/Android device; Android tests use a 360 dp wide device or emulator.
3. **Design tokens only** — every colour is one of the three defined tokens: `#F4F1EA` background, `#151515` text, `#FF5A1F` primary action. No other colour may be used without first adding it to `src/theme/tokens.ts`. Fonts are Archivo Black (headings) or IBM Plex Sans (body). Touch targets are at least 48 pt/dp. No gradients. Border radius 6 pt/dp everywhere.
4. **No secrets in the app bundle** — no OpenAI API keys, Supabase service-role keys (the private admin key), RevenueCat secret keys, or any other private credential in any TypeScript/JavaScript file or `app.config.js` that ships to users. Only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variables (anon key, public SDK keys) are permitted in the app.

---

## Milestone 1 — Project Skeleton & Device Access

**Goal of this milestone:** A blank but correctly configured app runs on your actual phone. Every later slice is tested the same way.

---

### M1.1 — Create Expo project and run on phone

**Goal:** "Hello FormCoach" boots on your phone via Expo Go, proving the entire toolchain works before writing any real code.

**Build prompt:**

