### M8.1 — In-app account deletion

**Goal:** Members can permanently delete their account from the Profile screen. Apple requires this for any app that lets users create accounts.

**Build prompt:**

```
Create supabase/functions/delete-account/index.ts:

import { serve } from 'https://deno.land/std@0.177.0/http/server.ts';
import { createClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2';

serve(async (req) => {
  const auth = req.headers.get('Authorization');
  if (!auth) return new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 });

  const userClient = createClient(
    Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_URL')!, Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_ANON_KEY')!,
    { global: { headers: { Authorization: auth } } }
  );
  const { data: { user } } = await userClient.auth.getUser();
  if (!user) return new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 });

  const admin = createClient(Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_URL')!, Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY')!);

  // 1. Delete all video files in storage under this user's folder
  const { data: files } = await admin.storage.from('videos').list(user.id);
  if (files && files.length > 0) {
    const paths = files.map(f => `${user.id}/${f.name}`);
    await admin.storage.from('videos').remove(paths);
  }

  // 2. Delete the user from auth.users (cascades to all public.* tables via ON DELETE CASCADE)
  const { error } = await admin.auth.admin.deleteUser(user.id);
  if (error) return new Response(error.message, { status: 500 });

  return new Response('Deleted', { status: 200 });
});

Deploy: supabase functions deploy delete-account --no-verify-jwt

In app/(tabs)/profile.tsx, add a "Delete account" button below "Log out":
  borderColor: colors.primary, borderWidth: 1, borderRadius: 6, minHeight: 48
  label: "Delete account" in fonts.body, color: colors.primary

  onPress:
    Alert.alert(
      'Delete account?',
      'This permanently deletes your account, all workouts, videos, and body measurements. This cannot be undone.',
      [
        { text: 'Cancel', style: 'cancel' },
        { text: 'Delete permanently', style: 'destructive', onPress: doDelete },
      ]
    );

  async function doDelete() {
    const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
    const res = await fetch(`${process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/delete-account`, {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${session!.access_token}` },
    });
    if (!res.ok) { Alert.alert('Error', 'Could not delete account. Try again.'); return; }
    await supabase.auth.signOut();
    router.replace('/auth/sign-up');
  }
```

**How to test:**
1. Create a throwaway test account. Log some data and upload a video.
2. Profile → "Delete account" → "Delete permanently."
3. App navigates to sign-up screen.
4. Supabase → Authentication → Users: test user is gone.
5. Supabase → Storage → videos: test user's folder is gone.
6. Trying to log in with the deleted account credentials fails.

**Done when:** Confirmation dialog shown. Account deleted from Auth. Storage files deleted. All table rows deleted via CASCADE. App navigates to sign-up.

